{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.VolumeForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CRRealisation","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SubstrateParameter"],"declarations":32,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SU2EmergenceDaggerUnitarity.unitary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SU2EmergenceDaggerUnitarity.unitary","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L125-L125","doc":"`g†` agrees with `g⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SU2EmergenceDaggerUnitarity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SU2EmergenceDaggerUnitarity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SU2EmergenceDaggerUnitarity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SU2EmergenceDaggerUnitarity","kind":"class","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L116-L125","doc":"**Dagger unitarity — typeclass.** Under the QOU hypotheses,\nevery tensor automorphism `g ∈ G` preserves the positive-definite\nFrobenius dagger on `τ(V)`; equivalently, `G ⊆ U(2)`. Per-`g`\nwitness pending the categorical-dagger formalisation.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{lem:su2-emergence-dagger-unitarity}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SU2EmergenceVolumeDeterminant.det_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SU2EmergenceVolumeDeterminant.det_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L114-L114","doc":"The determinant of `g_V` is 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SU2EmergenceVolumeDeterminant.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SU2EmergenceVolumeDeterminant.mk","kind":"ctor","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L112-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SU2EmergenceVolumeDeterminant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SU2EmergenceVolumeDeterminant","kind":"class","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L105-L114","doc":"**Volume determinant — typeclass.**  Under the QOU hypotheses,\nevery tensor automorphism `g ∈ G` of the fibre functor satisfies\n`det(g_V) = 1`; equivalently, `G ⊆ SL(2)`. Per-`g` witness\npending the categorical determinant formalisation in Mathlib.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{lem:su2-emergence-volume-determinant}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QYangMillsLevi.action_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QYangMillsLevi.action_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The action is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QYangMillsLevi.action_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QYangMillsLevi.action_value","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L99-L99","doc":"The total action value `S_q[A, θ]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QYangMillsLevi.integrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QYangMillsLevi.integrand","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L97-L97","doc":"The integrand `q(p) · ‖F_A⁺|_H‖²(p)` at each point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QYangMillsLevi.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QYangMillsLevi.mk","kind":"ctor","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QYangMillsLevi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QYangMillsLevi","kind":"structure","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L92-L101","doc":"**q-Weighted Yang–Mills–Levi functional**.\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:q-yang-mills-levi}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:q-yang-mills-levi","label":"def:q-yang-mills-levi","md":"quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/q-yang-mills-levi.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHodgeStar.star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHodgeStar.star","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L90-L90","doc":"The star operator `⋆_q : Ω^k(A) → Ω^{n−k}(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHodgeStar.forms_nk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHodgeStar.forms_nk","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L88-L88","doc":"The object of `(n−k)`-forms `Ω^{n−k}(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHodgeStar.forms_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHodgeStar.forms_k","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L86-L86","doc":"The object of `k`-forms `Ω^k(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHodgeStar.degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHodgeStar.degree","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The degree `k` of the forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHodgeStar.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHodgeStar.mk","kind":"ctor","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHodgeStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHodgeStar","kind":"structure","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L78-L90","doc":"**q-Hodge star** involution on differential forms.\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:q-hodge-star}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:q-hodge-star","label":"def:q-hodge-star","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-hodge-star.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SU2Emergence.det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SU2Emergence.det_one","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L76-L76","doc":"**Determinant-one constraint**: `det(g_V) = 1` for all `g ∈ G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SU2Emergence.ext_sq_action","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SU2Emergence.ext_sq_action","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The action of `G` on `Λ²V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SU2Emergence.groupInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SU2Emergence.groupInst","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L72-L72","doc":"`G` is a group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SU2Emergence.gaugeGroupType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SU2Emergence.gaugeGroupType","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The gauge group type `G = Aut⊗(ω)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SU2Emergence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SU2Emergence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SU2Emergence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SU2Emergence","kind":"structure","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L64-L76","doc":"**Emergence of the gauge group** (Theorem): `Aut⊗(ω) ≅ SU(2)`.\nLaTeX: `\\label{thm:su2-emergence}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.volumeIso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.volumeIso","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The volume form `ε : Λ²V ≅ 𝟙` — non-degenerate in the sense this\nlemma's own prose gives that word, `rank(Λ²V) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.projection_epi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.projection_epi","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The `↠` of the field above, formalised. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.projection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.projection","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The projection `π : V ⊗ V ↠ Λ²V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.exteriorSquare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.exteriorSquare","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The exterior square `Λ²V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.phi","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L53-L53","doc":"The symplectic isomorphism `φ : V ≅ V∨`.  The prose says `≅`; the field\nused to say `⟶`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.V_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.V_dual","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The dual object `V∨`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.V","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The fundamental object `V` of categorical dimension 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFromRigidity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFromRigidity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFromRigidity","kind":"structure","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/VolumeForm.lean#L22-L62","doc":"**Volume form from rigidity and symplectic self-duality.**\n\nAligned with condition (iii) of `QuantumObservableUniverse` under the iso\nreading (bean `qou-n1dj`, 2026-08-22).  The change is dictated by this\nlemma's **own prose**, which is where the corpus settles what\n\"non-degenerate\" means for this `ε`:\n\n> producing an epimorphism `ε : Λ²V → 𝟙`.  **For `ε` to be non-degenerate,\n> we must have `rank(Λ²V) = 1`.**\n\n`rank(Λ²V) = 1` is `C(N,2) = 1` is `N = 2`\n(`exteriorSquareDim_eq_one_iff`), so the author's own non-degeneracy\ncondition *is* the strong reading.  Previously `projection` and\n`volumeForm` were bare morphisms, and neither the `↠` of the docstring nor\nthe non-degeneracy of the prose was formalised at all.\n\nOne thing the prose overstates, which this structure deliberately does not\nrepeat: \"this alternating condition forces `rank(V) = 2`\".  An alternating\nform exists on every even rank; what forces `2` is the *next* sentence's\n`rank(Λ²V) = 1`.  So `phi` is recorded as the symplectic isomorphism it is,\nand the rank comes from `volumeIso`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{lem:volume-from-rigidity}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}